The ICO's own penalty notice names ZeroLogon (CVE-2020-1472), unpatched on two domain controllers and exploited during the incident though not the way in; only the Cl0p attribution comes from the press. The phishing foothold of September 2020 stayed dormant for 20 months before lateral movement and domain-admin compromise from May 2022, detection came on 15 July 2022, only 5% of the IT environment was monitored, and the fine is a UK GDPR penalty rather than an action under the Cyber Security and Resilience Bill.
